KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.variadic]/5 + [expr.new] -- pack expansion in a
new-initializer inside a FREE function template (the C++20
std::construct_at body).  With TWO or more forwarded arguments
constructing a class-template instance, the instantiated body fails to
convert ("no body for callee construct_at"); one argument works, and the
member-template flavour (__new_allocator::construct) is fixed
(cpp11_pack_expansion_new_init).  Bisection: neither constexpr nor the
decltype-SFINAE return type nor const members are needed; the trigger is
>= 2 pack args + a class-template target (j1/j6/j8 single-arg variants
pass, j4/j5/j7 multi-arg variants fail).  This is the remaining
front-end blocker of cpp20_map_basic: the C++20 headers construct map
nodes via constexpr allocator_traits::construct -> std::construct_at, so
the inserted key is never stored and the unbounded read-back diverges.
Flip to CORE when the free-function new-initializer pack expansion
handles multiple arguments.  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
